ations Expand\n\n### Affiliation\n\n  * ^{1} Wyss Institute for Biologically Inspired Engineering, Harvard University, Boston, MA 02115, USA.\n\n  * PMID: 24625926\n  * PMCID: PMC4153385\n  * DOI: 10.1126/science.1250944\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\n# Polyhedra self-assembled from DNA tripods and characterized with 3D DNA-PAINT\n\nRyosuke Iinuma et al. Science. 2014.\n\n\n. 2014 Apr 4;344(6179):65-9.\n\ndoi: 10.1126/science.1250944. Epub 2014 Mar 13.\n\n### Authors\n\nRyosuke Iinuma^{  1 }, Yonggang Ke, Ralf Jungmann, Thomas Schlichthaerle, Johannes B Woehrstein, Peng Yin\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nG-quadruplex-binding ligand-induced DNA synapsis inside a DNA origami frame - RSC Advances (RSC Publishing) (https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlelanding/2014/ra/c3ra45676e)\nciteturn90search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.9 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago;     https://doi.org/10.1039/C3RA45676E\n\n## G-quadruplex-binding ligand-induced DNA synapsis inside a DNA origami frame‡\n\nArivazhagan Rajendran,‡^{a}   Masayuki Endo,*^{bc}   Kumi Hidaka,^{a}   Phong Lan Thao Tran,§^{d}   Marie-Paule Teulade-Fichou,^{e}   Jean-Louis Mergny^{d}  and  Hiroshi Sugiyama*^{abc}  \n\nAuthor affiliations\n\n* Corresponding authors\n\n^{a} Department of Chemistry, Graduate School of Science, Kyoto University, Kitashirakawa-oiwakecho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto 606-8502, Japan\nE-mail: hs@kuchem.kyoto-u.ac.jp\nFax: +81-75-753-3670\nTel: +81-75-753-4002\n\n^{b} Institute for Integrated Cell-Material Sciences (WPI-iCeMS), Kyoto University, Yoshida-ushinomiyacho, Sakyo-ku, Kyoto 606-8501, Japan\nE-mail: endo@kuchem.kyoto-u.ac.jp\n\n^{c} CREST, Japan Science and Technology Corporation (JST), Sanbancho, Chiyoda-ku, Tokyo 102-0075, Japan\n\n^{d} Univ. Bordeaux, INSERM, U869, ARNA Laboratory, 2 rue Robert Escarpit, Pessac, France\n\n^{e} Institut Curie, UMR 176 CNRS, Campus Universitaire Paris-Sud, 91405 Orsay, France\n\n### Abstract\n\nAmong the approaches for DNA-based drug targeting, G-quadruplex-binding ligands are of particular interest because of the high abundance of G-rich sequences in regions such as human chromosomal telomeres and promoters of several proto-oncogenes. A number of quadruplex-ligands have been reported, but their functions at single-molecule level have not been explored using direct and real-time methods. Here, we report on the direct observation of the formation of a four-stranded G-quadruplex induced by bisquinolinium pyridine dicarboxamide with a linker containing biotin at one end. We fabricated a DNA origami frame with incorporated duplex DNAs that contained 3–6 G–G mismatches in the middle. In the absence of ligand, the duplex DNAs of interest had no interaction, as visualized by their parallel-shape in high-speed atomic force microscopy (HS-AFM) images. Presence of ligand induced the formation of G-quadruplex structure, which was characterized by an X-shape. Addition of streptavidin to the ligand-induced quadruplex caused the protein to localize in the middle of the X-shape, indicating that the ligand is bound to the quadruplex. A sequence of real-time images of the ligand-induced formation of a quadruplex and its reverse conformational switching by removing the ligand was captured by HS-AFM. Unprecedented intermediate-like states were recorded in our real-time analysis.\n\nImage: Graphical abstract: G-quadruplex-binding ligand-induced DNA synapsis inside a DNA origami frame\n\n## Supplementary files\n\n  * Supplementary movie AVI (915K)\n  * Supplementary information PDF (6040K)\n  * Supplementary movie AVI (845K)\n\n## Article information\n\nDOI\n    https://doi.org/10.1039/C3RA45676E\n\nArticle type\n    Paper\n\nSubmitted\n    09 Oct 2013\n\nAccepted\n    17 Dec 2013\n\nFirst published\n    20 Dec 2013\n\n### Download Citation\n\nRSC Adv., 2014,4, 6346-6355\n\n[Select] [Input]\n\n### Permissions\n\nRequest permissions\n\n### G-quadruplex-binding ligand-induced DNA synapsis inside